{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdvQUJePiKxQVz8T1QUT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The candidate passes the admission self-check, but that check doesn't test novelty or convergence. It completed the 100-draw smoke fit with a finite log-probability, met the data contract, and scored a finite ELPD-LOO of −3450.1 (the incumbent is at −3451.1).\n\n**Model:** `attentiveness_linked_pattern_gain`, a refinement of the incumbent `personal_pattern_detection_gain`.\n\n**The one change:** each person now has a single latent \"attentiveness\" trait that drives three of their personal parameters together, each through its own fitted loading:\n- how sharply they judge the switching rate against their ideal,\n- how strongly they notice structural cues (their pattern-detection gain),\n- how rarely they guess.\n\nIn the incumbent these three vary independently. Here, attentive people are consistent on every kind of pair and inattentive people on none. That predicts a wider spread in how often people agree with the majority, which is the critique's discrepancy that survives FDR. Everything else is the incumbent's code unchanged.\n\n**Risks for the full admission fit:**\n- **Unreliable LOO estimate:** on the smoke fit, 9.5% of trials had a high Pareto k, well above the 1% tolerance. That may just be because the run was short and used one chain, but if it holds in the full fit, this model's ELPD will be marked untrustworthy. It would then lose to the best trusted model at export and be among the first retired by the live-set cap.\n- **Convergence:** one chain can't report R-hat, so convergence is unverified. To pin down the sign of the attentiveness trait, I constrained its loading on switching sensitivity to be positive.\n- **Novelty:** if the fitted loadings come out near zero, its predictions could fall within the 0.002 RMSE threshold of the incumbent's and be rejected as a near-duplicate.\n\nFiles are in `experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_4/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":87343,"cache_read_input_tokens":11602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":87343,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9164ef38-7151-474e-824b-5d0916b56f3d","uuid":"afaefc5c-8a00-45fd-a0a2-31f6a831fa22","timestamp":"2026-10-02T18:57:16.499Z","request_id":"req_011CfdvQTpcmWiZma8XQnwa2"}
